sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/kimura-substitution-rate> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis>;
    dc:description "For neutral mutations the long-run rate of molecular substitution equals the mutation rate per generation, independent of population size, which yields a molecular clock.";
    dc:source "Motoo Kimura (1968) Evolutionary Rate at the Molecular Level";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Neutral substitution rate equals the mutation rate";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/351652a0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "k = 2N\\mu \\cdot \\frac{1}{2N} = \\mu";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: strictly neutral mutations, mutation rate constant per generation, steady state. Formal status: an exact consequence of the neutral fixation probability. Variation in generation time and weak selection on nearly neutral sites cause departures from strict clock-like rates.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Compare the substitution rate at putatively neutral sites (synonymous sites, pseudogenes) across lineages with independently measured per-generation mutation rates from pedigree sequencing."
}
